  <h2>Why Myeongdong?</h2>
  <p>Myeongdong is ground zero for K-beauty. Every major Korean skincare and cosmetics brand has a flagship or multi-story store here. The streets are pedestrianized at night, lined with food vendors, and alive with energy until past midnight. If you only have time for one shopping destination in Seoul — this is it.</p>

  <h2>K-Beauty Brands to Visit</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Olive Young</strong> — Korea's biggest beauty pharmacy. Best for variety — carries every major brand under one roof. Multiple Myeongdong locations.</li>
    <li><strong>Innisfree</strong> — Natural ingredient skincare. Jeju-inspired. Cult favorites include Green Tea Serum.</li>
    <li><strong>The Face Shop</strong> — Affordable, accessible skincare and makeup.</li>
    <li><strong>Etude House</strong> — Playful, colorful makeup for younger crowds.</li>
    <li><strong>Sulwhasoo / Laneige / HERA</strong> — Premium Korean skincare. Worth visiting for samples alone.</li>
    <li><strong>Cosrx</strong> — Global K-beauty darling. Snail mucin, acne patches, BHA toners.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="tip-box">
    💡 <strong>Ask for samples!</strong> Korean beauty stores give out samples generously — especially to tourists. Don't be shy to ask. Staff in Myeongdong typically speak basic English, Chinese, or Japanese.
  </div>

  <h2>Tax Refund in Myeongdong</h2>
  <p>Most stores in Myeongdong participate in Korea's <strong>immediate tax refund system (즉시환급)</strong>. Spend ₩30,000+ in a single store, show your passport, and get the 10% VAT refunded instantly at the counter — no airport wait needed. Look for the "Tax Free" or "즉시환급" sticker at the entrance.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Minimum purchase: ₩30,000 per store</li>
    <li>Refund: approximately 7–10% (after processing fee)</li>
    <li>Bring your passport — it's required</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Street Food in Myeongdong</h2>
  <p>From mid-afternoon, the pedestrian streets fill with vendors:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>🥚 <strong>Egg bread (계란빵)</strong> — Fluffy bread with whole egg, crispy edges</li>
    <li>🌀 <strong>Tornado potato</strong> — Spiral-cut deep fried potato on a stick</li>
    <li>🍢 <strong>Tteokbokki</strong> — Chewy rice cakes in spicy-sweet sauce</li>
    <li>🦑 <strong>Grilled squid</strong> — Fresh, seasoned, chargrilled</li>
    <li>🍡 <strong>Hotteok</strong> — Warm pancake filled with brown sugar, nuts, and cinnamon</li>
    <li>🧆 <strong>Gyeranppang</strong> — Mini egg cakes, sweet and light</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Department Stores & Duty Free</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Lotte Department Store Myeongdong</strong> — 9 floors, luxury brands, massive underground food hall</li>
    <li><strong>Shinsegae Department Store</strong> — Seoul's most prestigious department store, art installations throughout</li>
    <li><strong>Lotte Duty Free</strong> — Tax-free luxury goods. Must show passport and same-day departing flight ticket. Great for perfumes, cosmetics, designer goods.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Shopping Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Carry your passport everywhere — tax refunds require it</li>
    <li>Best time to visit: weekday evenings (less crowded than weekends)</li>
    <li>Card payments accepted everywhere; have cash for street food</li>
    <li>Compare prices across stores — Olive Young often beats individual brand stores</li>
    <li>Bring an extra bag — you will buy more than planned</li>
  </ul>

